                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0a95fe97-c3fc-3e06-921d-dabb4ae53874",
                        "entry_id": "8dfbca95-b444-3f2a-a607-d7b548485a7d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui tue son neveu."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Très rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6bf350cf-2d86-4e28-abad-f7729877f0bb",
                                "sense_id": "0a95fe97-c3fc-3e06-921d-dabb4ae53874",
                                "text": "Prenez garde, monsieur, votre conduite est odieuse, déjà tout le monde vous montre au doigt et dit en vous voyant : Cet homme est népoticide !"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ca5af95-5b0e-41a6-82a3-5cce651d0ddc",
                                "sense_id": "0a95fe97-c3fc-3e06-921d-dabb4ae53874",
                                "text": "Enfin cette chambre déjà tant attaquée à cause du jugement de Ney, vous la condamnez à devenir népoticide !"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "629af64a-69aa-3790-93e5-f401c81e45f5",
                "word": "népoticide",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6fabd125-625d-4048-b339-d2c6a34a48af",
                        "entry_id": "629af64a-69aa-3790-93e5-f401c81e45f5",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "népoticides"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1505a99a-c3a7-35f8-bdf3-1ac8b2f669aa",
                        "entry_id": "629af64a-69aa-3790-93e5-f401c81e45f5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Fait de tuer son neveu ; homicide de son neveu."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Très rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1442982e-7383-4480-a379-eb5c301c52ab",
                                "sense_id": "1505a99a-c3a7-35f8-bdf3-1ac8b2f669aa",
                                "text": "Le dénouement de Gabrielle de Vergy, le tocsin de Charles IX, le bûcher des Templiers, les fureurs d’Oreste, le parricide de Seïde, le fratricide de Caïn, le sororicide d’Horace, l’infanticide de Médée, le népoticide d’Atrée, le matricide d’Arsace, le régicide de Brutus, l’homicide du Cid et le suicide de Caton ne sont que des incidens à la rose auprès de la fin tragique de Catuat."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d48a0df-5fca-475f-bd0a-352b52678257",
                                "sense_id": "1505a99a-c3a7-35f8-bdf3-1ac8b2f669aa",
                                "text": "Une autre version qualifie ce meurtre de « parricide », ce qui est une exagération; un népoticide tout au plus."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c91c4727-846d-4532-a11a-8aa7efe7adb0",
                                "sense_id": "1505a99a-c3a7-35f8-bdf3-1ac8b2f669aa",
                                "text": "Les Atrides perpétrèrent les uns sur les autres toutes les formes possibles du parricide, du fratricide, de l’infanticide, du népoticide."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2de8cdd0-ea45-4031-8cb1-1f8d654b707b",
                                "sense_id": "1505a99a-c3a7-35f8-bdf3-1ac8b2f669aa",
                                "text": "Le népoticide commis par Yongle au mépris flagrant des instructions paternelles destinées à assurer une succession sans heurt l'exposa à un gigantesque déficit de légitimité. L’administration se montra sceptique, la population atterrée."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bbf8b1fd-413c-3fc7-bbe1-545847944fe0",
                        "entry_id": "629af64a-69aa-3790-93e5-f401c81e45f5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Personne qui tue son neveu."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Très rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0b6f2c3c-48d8-41a5-9706-aa47a9ddcf69",
                                "sense_id": "bbf8b1fd-413c-3fc7-bbe1-545847944fe0",
                                "text": "Les Annales d’Aquitaine, par Jean Besly, disent que ce roi étant au château de Chinon, où il avait attiré son neveu, jeta par une fenêtre le jeune prince, qui par sa mort laissa son duché à ce népoticide."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f3193da7-d055-4a9d-be48-92e4a90bbd3a",
                        "source_entry_id": "629af64a-69aa-3790-93e5-f401c81e45f5",
                        "target_lang_word": "nepoticide",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "nepoticide",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7f937982-b798-3cfd-9ddc-7a4ebaad038a",
                                        "entry_id": "6cccbbda-09f1-36ab-874e-4fc14d79d591",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The killing of one's own nephew."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14913661-9a4f-49c9-b2ff-64bc062d2dcf",
                                                "sense_id": "7f937982-b798-3cfd-9ddc-7a4ebaad038a",
                                                "text": "The new accusation brought by Urban against Manfred of murdering his sister-in-law's embassador – it may be observed that, tacitly, he acquits him of parricide, fratricide, and nepoticide – requires a little explanation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a9966ed-d074-4206-9f40-c2a90d1ff5e8",
                                                "sense_id": "7f937982-b798-3cfd-9ddc-7a4ebaad038a",
                                                "text": "[Charles] Dickens did not get to work out the interplay between these varying guardians and their various wards; and if the murder was to be a nepoticide, it remains forever shrouded by non-completion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bec558a0-ebf2-493e-9480-05aa9999d025",
                                                "sense_id": "7f937982-b798-3cfd-9ddc-7a4ebaad038a",
                                                "text": "The idea of parricide should be defined elastically enough not only to include avunculicide but to make it optional whether the youth or his father takes the initiative in expressing the antagonism between them. In the story from New Guinea, there is sexual jealousy between a father and son, and the father eventually kills the son instead of the other way around. In the Trukese story, we have an attempt at nepoticide, for the uncle tries to kill his nephew."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd927af8-aea2-4663-8ec3-8a7cb6e6ac75",
                                                "sense_id": "7f937982-b798-3cfd-9ddc-7a4ebaad038a",
                                                "text": "The Injuns get to Naturmitgefuhl by the metaphor of a family: if you don't throw the roe-plump squeteague back, that is a sort of nepoticide."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1dfccf5-79ca-46d1-a35f-287fb7841320",
                                                "sense_id": "7f937982-b798-3cfd-9ddc-7a4ebaad038a",
                                                "text": "Terms related to familicide include filicide (the killing of one's child or children), uxoricide (the killing of one's wife), fratricide or sororicide (the killing of one's brother or sister), avunculicide (the killing of one's uncle), and nepoticide (the killing of one's nephew)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1718f288-dbe6-430b-9f13-11c80f7f821e",
                                                "sense_id": "7f937982-b798-3cfd-9ddc-7a4ebaad038a",
                                                "text": "He was my nephew as well, so what is that? Fratricide is brothers. Filicide is sons. Nepoticide. That's the one."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a214da24-d254-3759-85a5-a00a418fa83f",
                                        "entry_id": "6cccbbda-09f1-36ab-874e-4fc14d79d591",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who kills his or her own nephew."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1939ea8-bbf5-460f-a964-f4dca789c8a0",
                                                "sense_id": "a214da24-d254-3759-85a5-a00a418fa83f",
                                                "text": "The fact that the Yongle emperor was therefore a usurper, regicide and nepoticide (nephew-killer) made compiling the Veritable Record – or official history – of his reign a most dangerous scholarly post. The official given this ticklish task managed to survive several drafts, finally producing one that pleased his master as it omitted the dead nephew's reign altogether."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
